-- infra/e2e/seed/55-phase3-batch2-miniapp-fixture.sql.tmpl
--
-- Deterministic tenant-DB fixture for infra/e2e/api-parity.mjs (Phase 3
-- batch 2 — mig-infra's extension of the JSON API parity harness). Covers
-- the 22 new endpoint x action pairs mig-api's two batch-2 briefs land:
-- appointments:{pharmacists,available_slots,book,my_appointments,cancel},
-- health-profile:{update_personal,update_medical_history,add_allergy,
-- remove_allergy,add_medication,remove_medication}, consent:save,
-- data-rights:{withdraw_consent,request_deletion,export_data},
-- medication-reminders:{list,add,delete,mark_taken}, and the 3 NEXT-ONLY
-- addresses:{list,upsert,delete} self-consistency cases (see
-- infra/e2e/lib/api-extract.mjs's NEXT_ONLY_CASES doc comment for why those
-- 3 are structurally separate from the 19 real PHP-vs-Next diff cases).
--
-- Applied by api-parity.mjs AFTER database/migration_2026-05-25_tenant_template.sql
-- + database/migration_2026-07-04_pdpa_data_rights.sql (both already applied
-- by the time this file runs — see api-parity.mjs's seedDatabase()) AND after
-- 45-phase3-batch1-plan-and-tenant.sql.tmpl + 50-phase3-batch1-miniapp-fixture.sql.tmpl
-- (this file REUSES that SAME tenant/line_accounts rows — line_account_id=1,
-- is_default=1 — it does NOT create a second tenant or re-seed line_accounts/
-- shop_settings). `USE __APP_DB_NAME__;` is prefixed by the harness itself,
-- same convention as 50-'s own file.
--
-- SCHEMA-DDL NOTE: no CREATE TABLE statements in this file. Every table this
-- fixture inserts into (appointments, pharmacists, pharmacist_schedules,
-- user_health_profiles, user_drug_allergies, user_current_medications,
-- user_consents, consent_logs, ai_conversation_history, transactions,
-- transaction_items, medication_reminders, medication_taken_history,
-- user_addresses) already exists in database/migration_2026-05-25_tenant_template.sql
-- (verified directly, cross-checked against mig-api's own contract doc
-- comments — see docs/runbooks/phase3-batch2-miniapp-api-parity.md §3) EXCEPT
-- `data_deletion_requests` / `users.deletion_status` / `users.deletion_requested_at`,
-- which come from database/migration_2026-07-04_pdpa_data_rights.sql
-- (applied by api-parity.mjs's seedDatabase() BEFORE this file — see that
-- script's own comment). This file therefore seeds DATA ONLY, same
-- "SCHEMA-DDL NOTE" precedent 50-phase3-batch1-miniapp-fixture.sql.tmpl's own
-- header already established for its batch.
--
-- IDENTITY STRATEGY: same "two separately-seeded identities suffixed -php/
-- -next" convention as batch 1 (see 50-...'s own header) for every WRITE
-- case. Every explicit numeric id below is chosen from a batch-2-only range
-- (4000s for `users`, 6000s for `appointments`/`user_drug_allergies`/
-- `user_current_medications`/`medication_reminders`, 900s for `pharmacists`)
-- that does NOT overlap any id 50-phase3-batch1-miniapp-fixture.sql.tmpl
-- already uses (3000s/500s/600s/700s/800s/5000s/8000s/9000s) — cross-checked
-- against that file directly, not by convention alone.
--
-- RELATIVE DATES: unlike batch 1's fixture (which could use fixed past
-- timestamps throughout, since read-only GETs never re-validate "is this in
-- the future"), a few rows here genuinely need to stay in the future (or
-- within a rolling 7-day window) FOREVER, no matter how long after this file
-- is written the harness actually runs — those use CURDATE()/NOW()-relative
-- SQL expressions instead of a fixed literal. Fixed PAST dates are safe to
-- hardcode forever (time only moves forward) and are used wherever "this row
-- must already be in the past" is the actual requirement.
--
-- ROUTING SIGNAL, EVEN WHEN THE HANDLER NEVER READS IT: several actions'
-- real PHP handler (and, correspondingly, the real line-mini-app client —
-- verified against line-mini-app/src/lib/{health-api,appointments-api}.ts)
-- never sends/reads `line_account_id` at all (health-profile's
-- remove_allergy/remove_medication, appointments' cancel). Both stacks'
-- tenant-resolution layer still needs SOME routing signal in the request
-- with no Host-pinning header (this harness's normal convention), so
-- infra/e2e/lib/api-extract.mjs's case bodies for those 3 actions add
-- `line_account_id` anyway — same precedent 50-...'s own fixture/extractor
-- established for member:update_profile ("line_account_id is REQUIRED here
-- even though the handler itself never reads it"). Flagged here, not
-- silently done, per this batch's own "document deviations" instruction.

