-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- addresses:{list,upsert,delete} — NEXT-ONLY self-consistency cases (NO PHP
-- source exists for this endpoint — see packages/contracts/src/addresses.ts's
-- own "PROMINENT FINDING" doc comment). ONE identity per case is sufficient
-- (no php/next split — each case makes exactly ONE HTTP call, not a
-- concurrent pair, so there is no twin-identity race to avoid). `list` gets
